// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// flists/xhb500_bridge_unit.flist
//
// The XHB500 bridge pair, and nothing else, for the standalone unit bench
// cocotb/xhb500_bridge.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-08-26)
//   The first coverage run measured `xhb500_axi_to_ahb_bridge_chiplet_mst_
//   core_xin` at FSM 0.00% in ALL 42 databases that contain it: no simulation
//   in this repository has ever driven an AXI AR or AW into the INBOUND
//   (peer-side) half of the cross-die path.  The `tidelink_top_pair_v2`
//   testbench does not model a peer-side XHB500 target memory, so the
//   inbound bridge can only be reached by instantiating it directly.
//
//   File ORDER and file SET are copied verbatim from the shipping tapeout
//   flist `tidelink_top_full_asic_v2.flist` (lines 87-121) so that this bench
//   compiles the SAME sources the ASIC does.  If those lines change, change
//   these -- a unit bench compiled against a different file set would report
//   coverage for RTL that does not tape out.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

